@issue-311 @packaging @cross-platform
Feature: Materialize packaged controller paths across hosts
  As a developer running a packaged nmg-sdlc command on a different host
  I want plugin-owned controller paths resolved from the active installation
  So that every packaged workflow starts the current host's controller

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Execute uses the installed Windows controller
    Given nmg-sdlc is installed on Windows
    And the packaged execute prompt contains a foreign POSIX path to "scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs"
    When the user runs "/sdlc-execute 19"
    Then Node invokes "scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs" beneath the active installed package root
    And the emitted invocation contains no foreign contributor-host path
    And controller startup does not fail with "MODULE_NOT_FOUND"

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Every packaged controller uses the active package root
    Given a packaged "<surface>" prompt invokes an nmg-sdlc-owned controller
    When the prompt is materialized using "<source path style>" on "<host>"
    Then the invocation uses the corresponding controller beneath the active installed package root
    And its existing arguments and workflow behavior are preserved

    Examples:
      | surface     | source path style | host    |
      | execute     | foreign POSIX     | Windows |
      | verify      | foreign Windows   | macOS   |
      | delivery    | canonical token   | Linux   |
      | interactive | canonical token   | Windows |
      | worker      | foreign POSIX     | Linux   |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Packaged artifacts stay host-neutral
    Given packaged workflow and file-command artifacts are generated or validated
    When repository contract checks inspect active commands, workflows, and shared references
    Then every plugin-owned controller invocation uses the canonical "<plugin-root>/scripts/<name>.mjs" representation
    And no contributor-host absolute nmg-sdlc controller path is accepted
    And each generated command remains byte-identical to its workflow source

  @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Project-local commands remain unchanged
    Given prompt text contains the project-local command "<command>"
    When plugin-controller path materialization runs
    Then the command remains byte-for-byte unchanged
    And the command is not redirected into the nmg-sdlc package

    Examples:
      | command                                      |
      | node scripts/check-gate.mjs                  |
      | node /opt/consumer/scripts/check-gate.mjs    |
      | node C:\consumer\scripts\check-gate.mjs      |

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Missing packaged controllers still fail closed
    Given an explicit plugin-owned reference names "scripts/missing.mjs"
    And the active package does not ship that controller
    When strict packaged-prompt materialization runs
    Then resolution fails with reason code "controller_unresolved"
    And no consumer-cwd or project-local fallback is consulted
